With employees based around the world, Magnet Forensics has been expanding our global presence. As a part of Magnet Forensics, you can expect to make a difference in the world, no matter what role you play. You’ll be supported through learning and development, not to mention an incredible team with unbelievable talent and integrity. 
 
If you think you would be the right person to join our team working towards this goal, we would love to hear from you! 


Role Overview 
We are looking for an experienced and impact-driven Senior Product Manager, Hardware to lead the strategy, roadmap, and lifecycle of our hardware products. Reporting to the Director, Product Management, this role is responsible for translating customer and business needs into a clear product vision and executable plans, while partnering closely with Hardware Engineering, Software Engineering, Operations, Supply Chain, Marketing and Support.  
 
This role is well-suited to someone with experience managing complex hardware products – often tightly coupled with software – and is comfortable navigating ambiguity, long development cycles, regulatory constraints, and operational trade-offs. You will act as a strong advocate for customer needs, balancing technical feasibility, cost, scalability, and time to market in partnership with cross-functional teams. 

What You'll Do



  Partner with engineering and design to build hardware products that make a real difference in people’s lives by helping to uncover the truth and protecting the innocent;  
  Collaborate on a highly visible product line with key business stakeholders including Executive Leadership, Sales, Marketing, Operations and Engineering to shape the vision for the product;  
  M  eet with Law Enforcement, Public Sector and Private Sector Leaders and customers in the Digital Forensics and Investigations domains to inform prioritization and product decisions;  
  Support go-to-market activities including positioning, pricing, launch readiness, and sales enablement;  
  Become the subject-matter expert in your product domain     



Role Responsibilities



  Own the product vision, strategy, and commercialization grounded in an extensive knowledge of our customers’ needs and competitors;  
  Fully understand market problems and use cases by gathering feedback from product stakeholders (i.e. Customers, Users, Internal Stakeholders) and observing market dynamics – always seeking to fully comprehend the core underlying pain or challenge;  
  Define clear customer and business outcomes, and be able to translate those into hardware deliverables and requirements, and drive them to delivery with cross-functional teams;  
  Contribute to long time portfolio and platform strategy where hardware is a differentiator;  
  Travel: 20%.     




What We're Looking For



  5+ years of experience in a Product Management role with significant ownership of hardware or hardware-centric products;  
  Strong understanding of hardware development lifecycles, including prototyping, validation, certification, and production;  
  Demonstrated customer empathy – recognizing and caring genuinely about the motivations, challenges and frustrations of our customers and advocating for solutions to resolve them;  
  Strong interpersonal communications skills - comfortable with presenting to customers, executive level stakeholders and other internal audiences;  
  Strong collaboration, critical thinking, and problem-solving skills with the ability to influence at all levels and create trust and strong relationships;   
  Bachelor’s Degree or College Diploma in a Technology Related Program, or equivalent practical experience.   



Nice to Have Skills



  Experience working on software products, particularly those tightly integrated with hardware  
  Prior experience in the Digital Forensics industry, Cybersecurity, or Law Enforcement.
